<title>USA: North Central Bancshares completes stock buyback.</title>
<headline>North Central Bancshares completes stock buyback.</headline>
<dateline>FORT DODGE, Iowa 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Central Bancshares Inc said Thursday it completed its second stock repurchase program, involving 381,050 common shares.</p>
<p>The bank holding company said it paid about $5.2 million for the stock, which was purchased on the open market. The last transaction is expected to be completed by December 24, at which point North Central said it will have more than 3.4 million common shares outstanding.</p>
<p>North Central is the parent of First Federal Savings Bank of Fort Dodge, a federally chartered stock savings bank.</p>
<p>The company's stock closed down 7/16 Thursday at 13-15/16.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
